Parts of this repository come from others and keep their own licenses:

- chips/*.h: Andre Weissflog's chips emulators, zlib license (the notice
  is in each file). chips/m6569.h, m6526.h, m6581.h and z80.h are altered
  versions, marked as such. chips/codegen: the code generator of z80.h
  from the same project (zlib license), altered too.
- chips/c64-roms.h: images of the Commodore 64 ROMs (BASIC, KERNAL,
  character generator). They belong to their copyright holders and are
  not covered by this license.
- chips/zx48-rom.h: the ZX Spectrum 48K ROM, copyright Amstrad plc.
  Amstrad have kindly given their permission for the redistribution of
  their copyrighted material but retain that copyright.
- carts/: Commodore's diagnostic cartridges (Dead Test, Diagnostic
  586220), which belong to their copyright holders, and the ZX Spectrum
  diagnostic ROM (LGPL 3). They are not covered by this license, see
  carts/LICENSE.
- third_party/sokol: zlib license. third_party/nuklear: MIT or public
  domain, at your choice (see the end of nuklear.h).
- src/c64_board_data.c: generated from bwack's C64-250407-Replica-KiCad,
  licensed under the CERN OHL v1.2.
- src/zx48_board_data.c: generated from liveboxandy's KiCad files of the
  ZX Spectrum 48K Issue 3B (CC0 1.0), redrawn from PABB's gerbers.
- src/ula.c is our own model of the Ferranti ULA, checked against the
  gate level netlist of the 6C001 recovered from the die by the
  emu-russia/ula project (CC0), which is not included here: see
  tools/ulacheck.c.

===========================================================================

THIS REPOSITORY (qtx-hw-sim)

This is an altered version of c64-hw-simulator
(https://github.com/antirez/c64-hw-simulator, by Salvatore Sanfilippo),
not the original: the simulator ported to Quartex Pascal, extended with
the Apple II+ and LC-80 boards and with a fast functional mode. The notice
above is the license of the original, unchanged; it applies to this
altered version as well. The additions of the port are:

Copyright (c) 2026 <your name>

and are licensed under the same terms as the notice above.

Parts of this repository come from others and keep their own licenses:

- src/hwsim.m6569.pas, hwsim.m6526.pas, hwsim.m6581.pas: ports of Andre
  Weissflog's chips emulators (chips/m6569.h, m6526.h, m6581.h, as altered
  by c64-hw-simulator), zlib license. src/hwsim.m6502.pas and
  hwsim.z80.pas are generated from chips' m6502.h and z80.h (zlib) by
  tools/gen_m6502.py and tools/gen_z80.py.
- src/hwsim.roms.pas holds ROM images that are not covered by this
  license:
  - the Commodore 64 ROMs (BASIC, KERNAL, character generator), which
    belong to their copyright holders;
  - the ZX Spectrum 48K ROM, copyright Amstrad plc. Amstrad have kindly
    given their permission for the redistribution of their copyrighted
    material but retain that copyright;
  - the cartridges of c64-hw-simulator's carts/ directory: Commodore's
    C-64 Dead Test and Diagnostic 586220, and the ZX Spectrum diagnostic
    ROM by Brendan Alford and contributors (LGPL 3). See
    LICENSES/cartridges.txt (c64-hw-simulator's carts/LICENSE) and
    LICENSES/zx-diagnostics.LICENSE;
  - the LC-80 monitor ROMs and the ROMs of the LC-80 variants (2716
    board, LC-80.2, LC-80e), which belong to their copyright holders.
- The Apple II+ ROMs are not in this repository: src/hwsim.roms_local.pas
  is an empty stub, and the Apple II+ runs its own test ROM until the
  ROMs are embedded locally (see README.md).
- src/hwsim.bd_c64.pas: generated from bwack's C64-250407-Replica-KiCad,
  licensed under the CERN OHL v1.2.
- src/hwsim.bd_zx48.pas: generated from liveboxandy's KiCad files of the
  ZX Spectrum 48K Issue 3B (CC0 1.0), redrawn from PABB's gerbers.
- src/hwsim.ula.pas is a port of c64-hw-simulator's model of the Ferranti
  ULA, checked against the gate level netlist of the 6C001 recovered from
  the die by the emu-russia/ula project (CC0), which is not included.
- data/apple2p/ and src/hwsim.bd_apple2p.pas: exported from a KiCad
  capture of the Apple II schematic of the Apple II Reference Manual
  (1979); see data/apple2p/README.md.
- data/lc80/lc80.pins.txt and src/hwsim.bd_lc80.pas: the LC-80 netlist,
  captured by hand from the schematic of the LC-80 (G-5403.500).
